{"type":"exercise","type_name":"Exercise","number":"","title":"A2","title_html":"A2","html":"<p>In <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"exm-gmm-qic\">@exm-gmm-qic</span>, QIC prefers independence\namong the working correlations but the AR(1) parameter is estimated at\n<span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"0.894\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2E\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c38\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c39\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c34\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0.894</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>. Are these two statements in\nconflict? Explain what each of them is measuring.</p>","file":"ch40-glmm-gee/05-working-correlation.html"}